{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-psa-105-1","title":"Psalms 105:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":105,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":105,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 An exhortation to praise God, and to seek out his works. 7 The story of God's providence over Abraham; 16 over Joseph; 23 over Jacob in Egypt; 26 over Moses delivering the Israelites; 37 over the Israelites brought out of Egypt, fed in the wilderness, and planted in Canaan.</p>\n<p>A.M. 2962. B.C. 1042. (Title.)It appears from 1Ch ch. 16, where the former part of this Psalm, as far as the 16th verse, is found with little variation, that David composed it at the removal of the ark to Mount Zion, and he himself probably enlarged it afterwards with the glorious detail of God's merciful dealings with Abraham and his posterity till their settlement in the land of Promise. The Hallelujah, which terminates the preceding Psalm, is made the title of this by the Septuagint, Vulgate, Arabic, and Ethiopic; and the Syriac considers it a paraphrase on the words, \"Fear not, Jacob, to go down into Egypt;\" \"and teaches us spiritually not to fear when we are obliged to contend with devils; for God is our shield, and will fight for us.\"</p>\n<p>Give. 136:1-3; 1Ch 16:7-22; 25:3; 29:13,20 call. Isa 12:4; Joe 2:32; Ac 9:14; Ro 10:13; 1Co 1:2 make known. 89:1; 96:3; 145:4-6,11,12; Nu 23:23; Isa 12:4; 51:10; Da 3:29 Da 4:1-3; 6:26,27</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-105-2","title":"Psalms 105:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":105,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":105,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>Sing unto. 47:6,7; 96:1,2; 98:1,5; Jud 5:3; Isa 12:5,6; 42:10-12; Eph 5:19 Re 15:3,4 talk ye. 77:12; 78:4-6; 119:27; Ex 13:8,9,14; De 6:6-9; Lu 24:14-53</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-105-3","title":"Psalms 105:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":105,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":105,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>Glory. 34:2; Isa 45:25; Jer 9:23,24; 1Co 1:29,31; Ga 6:14 let the heart. 9:10; Pr 8:17; Isa 45:19; 55:6,7; La 3:25; Lu 11:9,10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-105-4","title":"Psalms 105:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":105,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":105,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>Seek. Am 5:4-6; Zep 2:2,3 his strength. 78:61; 132:8; 2Ch 6:41 seek his face. 27:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-105-5","title":"Psalms 105:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":105,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":105,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>Remember. 77:11; 103:2; De 7:18,19; 8:2; 32:7; Isa 43:18,19; Lu 22:19 1Co 11:24-26 the judgements. 119:13; Re 16:7; 19:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-105-6","title":"Psalms 105:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":105,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":105,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>ye seed. Ex 3:6; Isa 41:8,14; 44:1,2; Ro 9:4-29 his chosen. De 7:6-8; Joh 15:16; 1Pe 2:9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-105-7","title":"Psalms 105:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":105,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":105,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>the Lord. 95:7; 100:3; Ge 17:7; Ex 20:2; De 26:17,18; 29:10-15; Jos 24:15-24 judgments. 48:10,11; Isa 26:9; Re 15:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-105-8","title":"Psalms 105:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":105,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":105,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>He hath remembered. 42; 111:5,9; 1Ch 16:15; Ne 1:5; Da 9:4; Lu 1:72-74 a thousand. De 7:9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-105-9","title":"Psalms 105:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":105,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":105,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>Ge 17:2; 22:16,17; 26:3; 28:13; 35:11; Ne 9:8; Ac 7:8; Heb 6:17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-105-10","title":"Psalms 105:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":105,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":105,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>an everlasting. Ge 17:7,8; 2Sa 23:5; Heb 13:20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-105-11","title":"Psalms 105:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":105,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":105,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>Unto thee. Ge 12:7; 13:15; 15:18; 26:3,4; 28:13 lot. Heb. cord. 78:55</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-105-12","title":"Psalms 105:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":105,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":105,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>a few. Ge 34:30; De 7:7; 26:5; Isa 51:2; Eze 33:24-33 and strangers. Ge 17:8; 23:4; Ac 7:5; Heb 11:9,12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-105-14","title":"Psalms 105:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":105,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":105,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>Ge 12:14-17; 20:1-7; 26:14-33; 31:24-29; 35:5; Ex 7:16,17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-105-15","title":"Psalms 105:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":105,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":105,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>Touch. Ge 26:11; Zec 2:8 mine. 1Ki 19:16; 1Jo 2:27 and do. Ge 20:7; 27:39,40; 48:19,20; 49:8-33</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-105-16","title":"Psalms 105:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":105,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":105,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>Moreover. Ge 41:25-32,54; 42:5,6; 2Ki 8:1; Am 3:6; 7:1-4; Hag 1:10,11; 2:17 Mt 8:8,9; Re 6:8 brake. 104:15; Ge 47:13,19; Le 26:26; Isa 3:1; Eze 4:16; Ac 7:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-105-17","title":"Psalms 105:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":105,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":105,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>He sent. Ge 45:5,7,8; 50:20 Joseph. Ge 37:27,28,36; 39:1; 45:4; Ac 7:9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-105-18","title":"Psalms 105:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":105,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":105,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>Whose. Ge 39:20; 40:15; Ac 16:24 he was laid in iron. Heb. his soul came into iron. 107:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-105-19","title":"Psalms 105:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":105,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":105,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>his word. 44:4; Ge 41:11-16,25; Pr 21:1; Da 2:30; Ac 7:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-105-20","title":"Psalms 105:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":105,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":105,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>Ge 41:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-105-21","title":"Psalms 105:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":105,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":105,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>made. Ge 41:40-44,55; 45:8,26 substance. Heb. possession.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-105-22","title":"Psalms 105:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":105,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":105,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>teach. Ge 41:33,38; Isa 19:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-105-23","title":"Psalms 105:23","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":105,"verseStart":23,"chapterEnd":105,"verseEnd":23},"content":"<p>Israel. Ge 45:9-11; 46:2-7; Jos 24:4; Ac 7:11-15 Jacob. Ge 47:6-9,28 the land. 27; 78:51; 106:22; Ge 10:6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-105-24","title":"Psalms 105:24","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":105,"verseStart":24,"chapterEnd":105,"verseEnd":24},"content":"<p>And he. Ge 13:16; 46:3; Ex 1:7; De 26:5; Ac 7:17; Heb 11:12 made. Ex 1:8,9; 12:37</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-105-25","title":"Psalms 105:25","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":105,"verseStart":25,"chapterEnd":105,"verseEnd":25},"content":"<p>He turned. Ge 15:13; Ex 9:16; 10:1; De 2:30; Ro 9:17-19 to hate. Ex 1:11-14,16; 2:23; Ac 7:19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-105-26","title":"Psalms 105:26","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":105,"verseStart":26,"chapterEnd":105,"verseEnd":26},"content":"<p>sent. 77:20; Ex 3:10; 4:12-14; 6:11,26,27; Jos 24:5; Mic 6:4; Ac 7:34,35 Aaron. Ex 7:1,12; 28:1,2,12,29-38; 29:5-46; Le 8:7-36 Nu 16:5-11,40,47,48; 17:5; 1Sa 12:6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-105-27","title":"Psalms 105:27","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":105,"verseStart":27,"chapterEnd":105,"verseEnd":27},"content":"<p>They. 78:43-51; 135:8,9; Ex 7:1-11:10; De 4:34; Ne 9:10,11; Isa 63:11,12 Jer 32:20,21 his signs. Heb. words of his signs. wonders. 23; 106:22</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-105-28","title":"Psalms 105:28","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":105,"verseStart":28,"chapterEnd":105,"verseEnd":28},"content":"<p>sent. Ex 10:21-23; Joe 2:2,31; Lu 23:44,45; 2Pe 2:4,17 rebelled. 99:7; Eze 2:4-8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-105-29","title":"Psalms 105:29","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":105,"verseStart":29,"chapterEnd":105,"verseEnd":29},"content":"<p>78:44; Ex 7:20,21; Isa 50:2; Eze 29:4,5; Re 16:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-105-30","title":"Psalms 105:30","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":105,"verseStart":30,"chapterEnd":105,"verseEnd":30},"content":"<p>brought. 78:45; Ex 8:3-14; Re 16:13,14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-105-31","title":"Psalms 105:31","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":105,"verseStart":31,"chapterEnd":105,"verseEnd":31},"content":"<p>there. 78:45; Ex 8:21-24; Isa 7:18 and lice. Ex 8:16-18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-105-32","title":"Psalms 105:32","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":105,"verseStart":32,"chapterEnd":105,"verseEnd":32},"content":"<p>them hail for rain. Heb. their rain hail. 78:47,48; Ex 9:18-28; Re 8:7; 11:19; 16:21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-105-33","title":"Psalms 105:33","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":105,"verseStart":33,"chapterEnd":105,"verseEnd":33},"content":"<p>Re 9:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-105-34","title":"Psalms 105:34","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":105,"verseStart":34,"chapterEnd":105,"verseEnd":34},"content":"<p>the locusts. 78:46; Ex 10:12-15; Joe 1:4-7; 2:25; Re 9:3-10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-105-36","title":"Psalms 105:36","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":105,"verseStart":36,"chapterEnd":105,"verseEnd":36},"content":"<p>He smote. 78:51; 135:8; 136:10; Ex 4:23; 11:4,5; 12:12,29,30; Heb 11:28 chief. Ge 49:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-105-37","title":"Psalms 105:37","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":105,"verseStart":37,"chapterEnd":105,"verseEnd":37},"content":"<p>brought. Ge 15:14; Ex 3:22; 12:35,36; Ac 13:17 and there.Considering the immense number of men, women, children, and cattle, it must certainly have appeared extraordinary, that there was none among them weak or feeble, none unable to perform the journey. The order was that \"not a hoof should be left behind;\" and He who commanded gave strength to obey.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-105-38","title":"Psalms 105:38","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":105,"verseStart":38,"chapterEnd":105,"verseEnd":38},"content":"<p>glad. Ex 10:7; 12:33 for. Ge 35:5; Jos 2:9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-105-39","title":"Psalms 105:39","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":105,"verseStart":39,"chapterEnd":105,"verseEnd":39},"content":"<p>spread. 78:14; Ex 13:21,22; 14:24; Nu 9:15-22; Ne 9:12,19; Isa 4:5 1Co 10:1,2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-105-40","title":"Psalms 105:40","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":105,"verseStart":40,"chapterEnd":105,"verseEnd":40},"content":"<p>asked. 78:18,26-28; Ex 16:12,13; Nu 11:4-6,31-33 satisfied. Ex 16:14-35; Nu 11:7-9; De 8:3; Jos 5:12; Ne 9:20 bread. 78:23-25; Joh 6:31-33,48-58</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-105-41","title":"Psalms 105:41","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":105,"verseStart":41,"chapterEnd":105,"verseEnd":41},"content":"<p>opened. 78:15,16,20; 114:8; Ex 17:6; Nu 20:11; Ne 9:15; Isa 48:21; 1Co 10:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-105-42","title":"Psalms 105:42","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":105,"verseStart":42,"chapterEnd":105,"verseEnd":42},"content":"<p>For he. 8-11; Ge 12:7; 13:14-17; 15:14; Ex 2:24; Lu 1:54,55,72,73 Abraham. Ex 32:13; De 9:5,27; Mic 7:20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-105-43","title":"Psalms 105:43","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":105,"verseStart":43,"chapterEnd":105,"verseEnd":43},"content":"<p>And he. 78:52,53; 106:8-12; Ex 15:13; De 4:37,38; Isa 63:11-14; Ac 7:36 Ac 13:17 with joy. Isa 35:10; 51:10,11; 55:12; Jer 31:11,12 gladness. Heb. singing. 106:12; Ex 15:1-21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-105-44","title":"Psalms 105:44","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":105,"verseStart":44,"chapterEnd":105,"verseEnd":44},"content":"<p>gave. 44:2,3; 78:55; 80:8; 135:10-12; 136:21,22; Jos 11:23; 21:43; 23:4 Jos 24:8,13; Ne 9:22-25 inherited. De 6:10,11; Jos 5:11; 13:7-33 the labour.That is, \"the produce of their labour;\" the cities and houses they had built, the vineyards they had planted, etc.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-105-45","title":"Psalms 105:45","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":105,"verseStart":45,"chapterEnd":105,"verseEnd":45},"content":"<p>That. De 4:40; 5:33; 6:1,2,21-25; Eze 36:24-28; Eph 2:8-10; Tit 2:14 Praise ye the Lord. Heb. Hallelujah. 106:1; 150:1; *marg: Re 19:3,4</p>"}]}